# the definition of `late` is put off: the variable holds a mark until somebody reads it, and nothing at all until the `const` is passed. `read` has a guard, a fast version and a slow one, and names a
# built-in, so the slow one is walked and not written straight. It is walked without Link's tables: nothing is proven of the variable there. "Nothing proven" of a variable with a dead zone is every
# value and no value yet: said as every value alone, the check of the dead zone passed by its type and was folded away, and the read by name took the empty word for a cell and died.
# f1 = read
# -- source: a-slow-version-asks-whether-a-definition-put-off-has-left-its-dead-zone.ts
